      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosts an annual Dean Martin Festival and houses a Dean Martin Room in the Jefferson County Historical Museum and Library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steubenville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Steubenville was founded in 1797 by Bezaleel Wells and James Ross, early settlers who built homes around the fort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofsteubenville.us/community/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Steubenville Female Seminary, founded in 1829 by Charles Clinton Beatty, was one of the first private women’s schools in Ohio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steubenville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city once boasted diverse industries—coal mining, paper mills, glass factories, potteries, nail factories, and steel mills—shaping its 19th‑century economy.",
